    confidence rollouts: confidence 0.4272   all features 0.4961   (+0.0689)
        random rollouts: confidence 0.6360   all features 0.6809   (+0.0448)

Read: if 'all features' clearly beats 'confidence only' (say +0.02 AUROC or more),
the extra features carry signal confidence misses, so the MLP has something to learn.
Within-step AUROC is the stricter test: a gain there means better choice of WHICH tokens
to commit; a gain only in pooled AUROC means better calibration across steps (useful for
deciding HOW MANY to commit with a threshold).
